     "markdown": "# Decision brief (draft): variant:triage=automated\n\n**Status:** draft for named human review. Approval records a decision for discussion only; nothing is deployed.\n\n- Pack: `insurance`; model `insurance-claims` v1.0.0, digest `09db5f2dd908b6d4`\n- Evidence: ledger record `experiment-c14ddb3c474d`\n- Narrative source: template-v1; grounding check: passed\n\n## Summary\n\nUnder the `normal` condition, cost per case incl. SLA penalty is 166.99 [F2] versus 186.50 [F1] for the baseline, lower than the baseline (an improvement); paired comparison. Under the `normal` condition, cost per completed case is 166.95 [F7] versus 186.50 [F6] for the baseline, lower than the baseline (an improvement); paired comparison. Under the `normal` condition, median cycle time (completed) is 2.13 [F12] versus 3.66 [F11] for the baseline, lower than the baseline (an improvement); paired comparison. Under the `normal` condition, p95 cycle time (completed) is 5.73 [F17] versus 7.81 [F16] for the baseline, with no clear difference from the baseline; paired comparison. Under the `normal` condition, completion rate is 98.9% [F22] versus 98.1% [F21] for the baseline, with no clear difference from the baseline; paired comparison. Under the `normal` condition, SLA attainment (open = miss) is 98.9% [F27] versus 98.1% [F26] for the baseline, with no clear difference from the baseline; paired comparison. These are simulated outcomes conditional on the stated assumptions.\n\n## Evidence table\n\n| Condition | Metric | Baseline | Alternative | Difference (95% CI) | Method | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| normal | cost per case incl. SLA penalty | 186.50 | 166.99 | -19.51 (-20.12 to -18.90) | paired | alternative |\n| normal | cost per completed case | 186.50 | 166.95 | -19.55 (-21.44 to -17.66) | paired | alternative |\n| normal | median cycle time (completed) | 3.66 | 2.13 | -1.53 (-3.04 to -0.03) | paired | alternative |\n| normal | p95 cycle time (completed) | 7.81 | 5.73 | -2.08 (-4.84 to +0.67) | paired | inconclusive |\n| normal | completion rate | 98.1% | 98.9% | +0.8 pts (-0.6 pts to +2.3 pts) | paired | inconclusive |\n| normal | SLA attainment (open = miss) | 98.1% | 98.9% | +0.8 pts (-0.6 pts to +2.3 pts) | paired | inconclusive |\n| normal | open cases at horizon | 19.3 | 10.5 | -8.83 (-24.19 to +6.52) | paired | inconclusive |\n| normal | manual escalations | 0.0 | 219.7 | +219.67 (+207.63 to +231.70) | paired | reference |\n\n## Constraint checks\n\n- normal: meets the decision rule (meets completion and SLA constraints on the mean)\n\n## Assumptions\n\n- `ins-a1` (synthetic-hand-authored): Arrivals are stationary Poisson over operating hours; no calendar.\n- `ins-a2` (synthetic-hand-authored): Automated triage sends 22% of claims to adjuster review (fallout).\n- `ins-a3` (synthetic-hand-authored): 8% of assessments need one more assessment pass (at most two extra).\n- `ins-a4` (synthetic-hand-authored): Staff are always available; no absenteeism or handoff delay.\n- `ins-a5` (synthetic-hand-authored): SLA miss penalty of 40 per case represents customer and rework cost.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- Results are simulated counterfactuals conditional on the stated operating model and assumptions; they are not causal estimates or forecasts.\n- Parameters are synthetic and hand-authored; no real operational data was used or validated.\n- Reviewing this brief changes nothing. A change can reach the sandboxed system of record only through a separately staged, approved and verified change package; no live system is connected.\n",
